n='tcp-congestion'
edit(n,'Above ssthresh, the sender is near the path\'s limit and probes gently: **cwnd grows by one MSS per RTT**.','In classic Reno congestion avoidance, the sender probes with approximately **one MSS of cwnd growth per RTT** under ideal ACK/traffic assumptions. Crossing ssthresh does not prove that the path is currently near capacity.','The threshold is algorithm state, not an observation of current spare capacity.',rfc(5681))
edit(n,'Sustaining full rate would need a loss rate below about one in five billion packets','In the distinct average-window model in RFC 3649, sustaining this average rate requires roughly one congestion event per five billion packets','Separate average-window model from peak-window recovery calculation.',rfc(3649))
edit(n,'Pacing gain about 2.89; doubles like slow start until the delivery rate stops growing','Pacing gain about 2.89, designed for rapid growth; exits after three qualifying rounds without 25% bandwidth growth','Exact BBRv1 pipe-full test is less than25% growth across3 eligible rounds, not zero growth.',['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/v6.12/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c'])
edit(n,'the sender keeps in flight at most min(cwnd, rwnd), so rate ≈ cwnd / RTT.','both windows constrain ordinary new-data sending. A continuously backlogged, cwnd-limited steady flow has rate ≈ cwnd / RTT.','Window reductions cannot instantaneously remove flight; rate approximation needs stated limiting assumptions.',rfc(5681))
edit(n,"Reno's linear growth can't fill fast, long paths; CUBIC grows as a cubic function of time since the last loss and backs off by 30%.","Reno’s linear growth can recover very slowly on high-BDP paths. CUBIC uses a time-based cubic target, a Reno-friendly region and normally a 30% congestion-event reduction.","Avoid absolute impossibility and distinguish cubic target from actual ACK-driven evolution.",rfc(9438))
qreplace(n,9,'options.0.explanation','double from 1 to ~65,000 segments (about 17 RTTs)','grow from 1 to at least 83,333 segments (17 ideal doubling rounds)','2^16=65536 while17doublings=131072; align arithmetic with target.')
n='tcp-performance'
qedit(n,2,'options.3.explanation','A small receive window can limit that connection’s sending allowance, but it does not by itself explain the observed load-correlated ping delay. A shared uplink queue is the leading hypothesis; queue classes and traffic paths determine which packets are affected.','Remove universal all-traffic queue impact and unsupported pings-to-everywhere statement.',rfc(8290))
qedit(n,3,'options.1.explanation','QUIC removes the requirement for a stream to wait solely for another stream’s missing bytes. Shared flow control, congestion control and application dependencies can still delay delivery. TCP uses one ordered byte stream.','Immediate QUIC delivery is not guaranteed.',rfc(9000))
qedit(n,3,'options.3.explanation','TCP handles this gap on the existing connection. The supplied scenario does not imply that the browser opens a replacement connection; doing so would require application-level recovery logic.','Avoid universal browser behavior claim.',rfc(9293))
qreplace(n,5,'workedExample','Distance and loss compound. This is a core reason CDNs put servers near users.','The model’s RTT and loss factors compound. Closer servers can reduce propagation delay, but geographic distance alone does not determine RTT or measured throughput.','Do not equate RTT with distance.',rfc(3649))
qreplace(n,8,'options.3.explanation',"The senders' congestion control then shrinks their windows.","Responsive senders can reduce their offered load; the response depends on the protocol, controller and delivered feedback.",'AQM does not force every sender to use a window or respond.',rfc(8289))
qedit(n,10,'options.3.explanation','The base TCP header allows up to40 option bytes. That finite space can constrain extensions too, but it is not zero; unfamiliar-option handling by middleboxes is a separate deployment obstacle.'.replace('up to40','up to 40'),'Option space is limited and can itself be an obstacle.',rfc(9293))
n='tcp-sockets'
qedit(n,3,'options.3.explanation','TCP checksums cover segments, independently of application message framing. They may be computed by the protocol stack or hardware offload; a kernel implementation is not required.','Avoid claiming all TCP checksums computed in kernel.',rfc(9293))
qedit(n,6,'options.3.explanation','Exhaustion of automatically selected local ports is a different failure mode. Here the supplied diagnostics identify retained TIME_WAIT state affecting an explicit bind; an existing conflicting allocation can also matter when a chosen fixed port overlaps the automatic range.','Fixed-port listeners can be affected by actual ephemeral allocations; diagnose supplied scenario.',['https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/ip.7.html'])
qedit(n,8,'options.0.explanation','Threads can call recv(); in CPython’s usual GIL-enabled build, blocking socket I/O releases the GIL. Replacing each native thread with a process adds separate process-management costs and does not remove the need to measure resource limits.','Version/runtime scope and remove unmeasured categorical capacity comparison.',['https://docs.python.org/3/library/socket.html'])
qedit(n,11,'options.1.explanation','Not reading replies does not itself require an immediate BrokenPipeError. Queued output can grow while the connection remains usable; independent failures or later endpoint closure are still possible.','Absence of reader does not prove no concurrent error.',rfc(9293))
